Subject: [PATCH] fritchii-nopersp: screen-linear (noperspective) varyings written times Position.w and read

fritchii-nopersp: screen-linear (noperspective) varyings written times Position.w and read
perspective-correct times FragCoord.w.
Switch EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_NOPERSP=1, off by default (Common::PeSwitch).

Upstream: zortos293/Lichii#820 (port of #722 by justin-wq1337), in Frizti/Fritchii v5 via
f9c0e2d611 "Port four small fixes from zortos293/Lichii build 125", 4th item ("the AMD red line in
the Royal Family's Tomb"; the Fritchii owner also saw Kakariko graveyard bushes stop flashing).

What: the last pre-rasterization stage writes each generic output the fragment program reads
noperspective times Position.w; the fragment stage reads it with perspective interpolation times
FragCoord.w. That is the interpolation the spec defines for a clipped primitive, and it avoids the
driver's noperspective clipping path (traced with RenderDoc to a wrong water-box depth on an RX
7800 XT). Kept native: transform feedback (it would capture scaled values), passthrough geometry
shaders, fragment programs with indexed attribute loads, and fragment programs after a mesh
program (our mesh-as-compute paths included: their previous program is Stage::Mesh). Geometry
shaders restore the unscaled outputs after each EmitVertex.

Files: runtime_info.h (noperspective_outputs, scaled_noperspective_inputs), spirv_emit_context.h/.cpp
(DefineInputs: forced FragCoord, no NoPerspective decoration on marked inputs),
emit_spirv_special.cpp (scale in EmitEpilogue for VertexB/TessEval and around EmitVertex),
emit_spirv_context_get_set.cpp (multiply by FragCoord.w on load), vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
MakeRuntimeInfo (fills the two fields).

Deviations from upstream:
- Switch-gated in MakeRuntimeInfo (Lichii #722's EDEN_NX2_NOPERSP_AS_SMOOTH idea; #820 itself is
  unconditional). Unset, both runtime fields stay empty: ScaleNoPerspectiveOutputs returns before
  emitting anything, DefineInputs decorates NoPerspective and defines FragCoord exactly as before,
  so SPIR-V is byte-identical.
- One hunk moved by hand: our DefineInputs position test has no info.passthrough term, so the new
  condition is `loads.AnyComponent(PositionX) || noperspective_as_smooth`.

With the switch on: every vertex/tess/geometry + fragment pair with noperspective inputs gets new
SPIR-V (one-time RADV compile) and one multiply per scaled component on each side. Pipelines are
cached as guest environments and re-emitted, so toggling the switch needs no cache clear.

PS5: medium value, late in the game (Royal Family's Tomb, Kakariko graveyard). The root cause is
the RDNA clipping path for noperspective varyings, plausibly the same under RADV; not seen on the
PS5 yet because that area hasn't been reached.

